{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D41-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d3cc704115f66ed8d9d2e8522be06b6f75193b99bd23626de62c95a1f82269bd\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 calls the cupboard finished; A3 and A5 redescribe missing functionality as deliberate design.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's opening question produces A3's surface appreciation; B4's failed opening becomes A5's security claim.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants usable storage, and B4 tests A's claim rather than merely accepting the sales pitch.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 converts B4's complete failure of access into an additional supposed benefit.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's finished, handle-free cupboard establishes a concrete handover that B2 immediately tests.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'uninterrupted surface' and A5's 'exceptionally secure' sustain one concise design defense.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your cupboard is finished. I've chosen a handle-free design.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How do I open it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"By appreciating the uninterrupted surface first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It won't open.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then the storage is exceptionally secure.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D41 turns incomplete or improvised work into a supposedly thoughtful finished version.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic positive reframing can praise a problem without claiming that unfinished work constitutes completion.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 explicitly declares completion, and A3–A5 defend the cupboard's unusability as intentional design.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative defends a physical product through invented benefits; D41-single-b recategorizes a scant deliverable as conceptual completion.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading: both discoveries change A's defense, and the original clears the rubric without requiring new material.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The missing construction step remains implicit; actors must understand that A's design language covers incomplete work.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D41-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"42801c65b813c8af9c1102a0179da9af7dfa6ef87046aa05fa556397ccbf5681\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 declares a numberless report complete; A3 and A5 successively redefine what has been finished.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 makes the numbers essential, prompting A3's 'supporting structure'; B4's title page prompts A5's 'vision'.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 credibly inspect a colleague's inadequate report and remove successive defenses.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 retreats to calling the title page a vision, but adds little consequence beyond A3's reclassification.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a report handover, and B4 supplies the immediately playable title-page reveal.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'supporting structure' efficiently bridges B2's correction to A5's smaller claim of completion.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 85\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The report's complete apart from the numbers.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The numbers are the report.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I've finished its supporting structure.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There's just a title page.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A clear vision. Most reports lack one.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D41 redescribes incomplete work as an intentionally complete version of a smaller or different achievement.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary excuse-making explains why work is missing; this card claims the remaining work already represents thoughtful completion.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 calls the missing report a finished supporting structure; A5 turns the sole title page into a completed vision.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike the cupboard maker's functional-benefit claims, this worker progressively narrows the definition of the deliverable.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained at the acceptance threshold: rereading confirms that each factual correction produces a specific new completion claim.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 heightens conceptual retreat more than practical stakes; its final generalization is less sharp than the title-page reveal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D42-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"28b91997a1368bf739693fd33c908f95d148189b4ac3c8a230948e363d27d6c3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 absorbs B2's steam correction while preserving expertise, but A5 claims to test B instead of clearly learning the cup step.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's steam information; A5 acknowledges B4's sequence but does not say what A now does with the cup.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 corrects a mistake and B4 offers practical help, giving A credible opportunities to bluff familiarity.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the expertise defense through 'checking you' without developing the coffee-making task.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 names the coffee machine, and B2's steam button makes the error immediately playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'warming up' is an economical cover; A5's testing claim is more familiar and less task-specific.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 79\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll make your coffee. I know this machine: this button starts it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That's steam. The coffee button is behind the flap.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Naturally. Steam first, then the concealed coffee controls. Where's your cup?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Here. It makes two cups unless you turn that dial.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. Dial to one. I always tailor the standard procedure to the guest.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D42 incorporates each newly supplied operating clue while presenting the resulting discovery as familiar procedure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Bluffing expertise alone can deny errors without learning anything about the task.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"The original A3 uses the steam clue, but original A5 mainly asserts authority; revised A5 explicitly uses B4's dial instruction.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This host folds helpful operating advice into personalized service; D42-single-b uses a camping partner's discoveries to maintain calm leadership.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the coffee setting to make learning explicit. Internal reread scores fidelity/logic/relationship/heightening/specificity/wit 5/5/4/4/5/4, total 92; B4's two-cup default causes A5's tailored dial setting. Five spoken turns and the word limit pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The concealed controls and dial are illustrative machine features; the performance still needs understated confidence rather than obvious deception.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D42-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"308159196d2287ceead8c97d83b44ace94c472f69b32a6edc093d67cc74bb9e7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 covers B2's correction with 'Testing'; A5 claims familiarity without learning any further tent operation.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 acknowledges B2 indirectly, while B4 supplies an accusation rather than a practical clue for A5.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 helps identify a component, but B4 shifts to exposing A and A5 simply demotes B to assistant.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'observant assistant' adds a status joke without advancing the tent task established in A1.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a tent, but B2's unexplained groundsheet rod makes the physical construction harder to picture.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 are short, but both use generic covers that could fit many unrelated tasks.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 57\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We'll have this tent up before the rain. I'm familiar with these sleeves.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"This one has clips. The poles cross first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes, the clip system. Cross the poles; then we attach the fabric.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That fabric's the outer cover. We're standing on the inner tent.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. Step off the inner tent and we'll raise it first. I always lay everything out.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D42 makes the character learn the task from fresh clues while treating each adjustment as established know-how.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A status-preserving comeback can sound confident without showing any acquired practical knowledge.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 only labels B an assistant; revised A3 learns the clips and revised A5 changes assembly order from B4's fabric identification.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The tent alternative adds shared weather pressure and an embarrassing physical discovery; the coffee alternative presents learning as attentive hospitality.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the whole camping exchange to replace exposure-only dialogue with useful clues. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/5/4, total 92; B4 causes A5 to step off and raise the inner tent first. Spoken-turn and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The outer/inner confusion is broad physical comedy; a calm delivery is necessary to preserve performed familiarity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D43-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"990bd058416266c45948857f0ccda53454da92b31b1b68420ca8b481c691dd76\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 overrepays dinner with all the dishes and A5 offers repainting, though restoring a competitive lead is only implied.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's soup to name spoons, but B4's 'just eat' does not specifically cause A5's dining-room repaint.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 minimizes the favor and B4 wants A to eat, but neither intervention changes the practical repayment tactic.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 enlarges dishwashing into repainting, but that escalation is not earned by B4's request.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and B2 establish a soup delivery; ownership and location become less clear when A5 names the dining room.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'match your kindness' explains the exaggeration, while the repainting itself could follow almost any favor.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 64\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You brought soup? I'll cook your dinners all week.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You're ill. I've already filled your freezer.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then when I'm better, I'll fill yours twice.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Mine's tiny. Just return the tubs.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. I'll bring them back full, with a bigger freezer. That should put me ahead.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D43 treats another person's help as an effort to surpass with a larger returning favor.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Excessive gratitude can overrepay kindness without seeking to regain the lead in giving.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 and A5 offer disproportionate favors; revised A5 explicitly seeks to get ahead through a larger gift caused by B4.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative turns care during illness into domestic overgiving; D43-single-b turns a colleague's lift and shift help into competing workplace sacrifices.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added illness and freezer details to the existing food-delivery setting. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/5/4, total 92; B4's tiny freezer causes A5's appliance offer, making the escalation specific. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The bigger freezer is deliberately extravagant, and the explicit 'ahead' phrase makes the competitive motive unusually overt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D43-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ee6e5634dc6f2d91d7d1d89c1e01553b6a0c4450a3f34c3f2f9737f44c2741ed\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 offer increasingly larger shift favors, and A5 names being ahead, but no new sacrifice follows B4.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's ten-minute duration through 'efficient generosity'; A5 treats B4's excess objection as success.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 credibly resist disproportionate repayment but provide little beyond successive minimization.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 declares victory over the lift rather than increasing or changing A3's two-weekend commitment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's lift and weekend shift establish coworkers exchanging favors, though no scheduling cost becomes concrete.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'efficient generosity deserves scale' states the premise abstractly; A5 largely summarizes it.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the lift. I'll cover your Saturday shift.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"No need. I covered yours yesterday so you could rest.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll take your whole weekend. You shouldn't be doing more than me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've already swapped Sunday to drive you to the airport.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll cancel my flight and cover your holiday. You deserve the longer break.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D43 answers each newly revealed sacrifice with a costlier sacrifice intended to recover the giver's lead.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Fair exchange tries to settle a debt; this drive keeps increasing repayment until A has given more.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 doubles the repayment and A5 mentions being ahead; revised A3 expressly rejects B doing more and A5 sacrifices the trip.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike the soup scene's escalating gifts, this scene makes the contest costly through work coverage and a canceled journey.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised B into an active giver whose additional sacrifices demand new responses. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/5/5/4, total 95; B4's airport sacrifice causes A5 to surrender the trip and cover B's holiday. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Canceling the flight is an extreme commitment; its sincerity must remain playable rather than sounding like a sarcastic threat.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D44-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"33e85329bd7a103cba150e5f941bfcb59528b8e789c3ebb1cb64fb51fd808941\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 turns a broken lift into canceling the gym, and A5 makes shopping part of the cheaper exercise routine.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's eight floors becomes A3's full programme; B4's shopping becomes A5's resistance training.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 raise credible shared-household burdens that force A to extend the proposed routine.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 incorporates carrying shopping into the plan and commits both residents to membership savings.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's broken lift and B2's eighth-floor home make the inconvenience and invented alternative concrete.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's rent-inclusive programme and A5's resistance training derive compactly from the same stairs.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The lift's broken. We can cancel the gym and use the stairs.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We live eight floors up.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A full programme included in the rent.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How do we carry the shopping?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Resistance training. We've saved two memberships.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D44 celebrates inconvenience as the trigger for inventing a cheaper, faster, or smarter routine.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic optimism finds a silver lining without changing how anyone does the recurring task.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 proposes replacing paid gym visits with stairs, and A5 integrates B4's groceries into that replacement routine.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative combines existing chores to cut recurring costs; D44-single-b redesigns serving dinner to eliminate washing.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading because both practical objections supply the next component of the same efficiency invention.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 assumes both people have memberships; the shared gym reference in A1 supports this but does not establish it explicitly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D44-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0718f87695226802d2517c686bcbf1a9a3b9278e8267954da6ef62f96d965aea\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A5 invent ways to avoid dishes, but A3's fewer introductions is not a clear routine improvement.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 invokes guests from B2 without explaining the introduction saving; A5's sandwiches do not necessarily answer B4's desire for plates.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 protects hosting standards and B4 makes the guests' likely needs concrete.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 changes the menu, but its claimed improvement leaves B4's plate objection partly unresolved.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a broken dishwasher and dinner plan; A3 makes the resulting social arrangement harder to picture.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's introductions line feels imported, whereas A5's 'system keeps improving' states the intended game.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 71\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The dishwasher's broken. Excellent: we'll serve the curry in rolls. No plates to wash.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There are twelve guests and only six rolls.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Halve them. Open sandwiches: twice the servings, same bread.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The curry will run off.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Hollow them out first. Edible bowls, and the crumbs thicken the curry. We've saved the flour too.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D44 treats each practical obstacle as evidence that another resource-saving routine can be invented.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Improvising a workaround alone lacks the card's celebratory claim that the inconvenience improves the system.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 links breakdown to shared-pan service; revised A3 saves bread and revised A5 saves both dishes and thickener.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative makes B a practical collaborator testing a meal redesign; the lift scene turns household burdens into a replacement fitness routine.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the broken-dishwasher dinner setting and added concrete food constraints. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/5/4, total 92; B4's runoff causes A5's hollow bowls and crumb reuse. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The serving plan is comic household ingenuity rather than a demonstrated recipe; the final line carries several related savings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D45-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ec2635b25119cac26d9f51357d2d7d37ecaa589df13cf0a5646c3e903c492285\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 accommodates another guest and A3 excludes the host from 'everyone arriving'; A5 makes hunger explicit but strains graciousness.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's food concern, and A5 declines B4's food offer, though the refusal lacks a specific accommodating reason.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 checks the burden and B4 sincerely offers to solve it, making B more than a source of demands.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 states the hunger already implied by A1 rather than showing inconvenience growing after B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 clearly establishes an extra dinner guest, but B4 leaves the timing and feasibility of bringing food open.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'what hosting tastes like without eating' is a crafted aphorism that risks overt sarcasm.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 75\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course your brother can stay for dinner. I'll give him my pie.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You haven't eaten either.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Please don't worry. There are peas, and I had a substantial breakfast.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll order you a pizza. It takes forty minutes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"How thoughtful. I'll keep everyone company while they eat, then you can all watch me have dinner at nine.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D45 preserves gracious accommodation while making the accumulating personal cost conspicuous.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Open resentment or guilt-tripping can advertise suffering while dropping the required gracious, accommodating surface.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 offers a portion and A5 announces hunger; revised A5 accepts B4's help warmly while exposing the resulting late, solitary meal.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This host accepts a helpful solution that extends the inconvenience; D45-single-b continues carrying a bag while exposing the increasing physical burden.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the existing dinner situation to give B's solution a concrete time cost. Internal reread scores 5/5/4/4/5/4, total 92; B4's forty-minute wait causes A5's gracious account of dinner at nine. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The last clause can still become pointed if delivered bitterly; the actor should mean the invitation to keep company.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D45-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"745c2bec8605f43747db8dd60bd513b0e1e0a43b2fabe790d7e258cd3ba27abf\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers to carry the bag, but A3's 'weight of your hobbies' sounds accusatory and the inconvenience does not clearly grow.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 refuses B2's offer to take the bag, and A5 specifically turns B4's books into a spine joke.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers relief and B4 defends the contents; A3 supplies little gracious reason to continue helping.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"e